{
  "title": "Compile 30–40 Seattle/PNW-prioritized climate/sustainability angels & seed VCs",
  "content": "## Deliverable\nA qualified list of **30–40 active Angel Investors and Seed VCs** that invest in **Sustainability, Climate Tech, and/or Circular Economy**, **prioritizing Seattle/PNW presence**.\n\n## Qualification rubric (applied to every entry)\nEach investor must have evidence for:\n- **Stage**: angel / pre-seed / seed (or explicitly early-stage)\n- **Thesis**: climate, sustainability, circular economy, decarbonization, clean energy, industrial sustainability, food/ag, built environment, carbon, etc.\n- **Activity**: proof of recent investing (e.g., recent portfolio additions, recent fund, recent announcements, current team roles)\n- **Geo signal**: Seattle/PNW office, partner presence, frequent PNW deals, or explicit interest in PNW\n\n## Output fields per investor (standardized)\n- Name (person or firm)\n- Type (Angel / Seed VC / Micro-VC / Angel syndicate)\n- Location + Seattle/PNW presence signal\n- Check size / stage focus (if available)\n- Climate/sustainability thesis keywords\n- Evidence of activity (date/source)\n- Example climate/sustainability portfolio companies (1–3)\n- Source links (website + 1–2 credible references)\n\n## Approach\nRun 4 parallel research tracks (PNW seed VCs, PNW angels/syndicates, national climate seed funds with PNW presence, and strategic/impact funds active at seed). Then dedupe, verify, and format into one ranked list prioritizing Seattle/PNW proximity and climate/circular relevance.",
